{"kind":"assert","text":"Revision of condition 1 of this request (a008a94d), by its author. The condition said the stale-read distinction applies on the attach path as well. Withdraw that clause: gs attach keeps the strict rollback rule it has today, and only the read path (Workspace.rememberVerifiedFrontier) admits a verification shorter than the witness. Reason: attachment is a ref-import with an expected-ref compare-and-swap, so a candidate shorter than a witness the ref continues can only pass the CAS if the ref was rolled back to exactly the expected head inside the window; admitting it there would trade a refusal that happens before the ref update for nothing, and the independent review found exactly that. Condition 1 now reads: checkVerifiedFrontier keeps the strict rule for attach; a read-path judgement distinguishes a stale read, where the current sequence ref continues the stored witness head, from a rollback, where it does not, and admits the first without moving the witness. Conditions 2 to 5 are unchanged. The reporting artifact for the head under review should rest on this revision."}